  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Targeted advocacy and community engagement to  Imprest Request No. 16</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">the project is designed to cover key aspects such as targeted advocacy of the legislature to enact the Code for Marketing Breastmilk Substitutes (CMBS) and follow-up with District Councils to incorporate nutrition and food security interventions into their District Annual Development Plans. Relevant Departments and Agencies in key line sector ministries like Health &amp; Sanitation, Agriculture and Food Security; Trade &amp; Industry and Information, will also be targeted through select advocacy briefings to keep them abreast with issues hinging on the CBMS, food security, infant and maternal wellbeing to influence their decision-making processes on such issues.</narrative>
  </description>
